  "interpretation": "Binarization (probit model, p=0.7) distorts variance component magnitudes with overall MAPE=49.3% across all 22 components. The distortion is highly non-uniform: (1) Residual inflates from 16% to 41% (pct_error=156%), absorbing Bernoulli within-cell variance \u2014 this is the expected and dominant effect of binarization. (2) item_id compresses from 50% to 32% (pct_error=36%), as Bernoulli noise dilutes true item differences. (3) Facet \u00d7 item interactions are best preserved (MAPE=12.8%), ranging from 8.7% (ordering:item_id) to 17.5% (temperature:item_id). (4) Main effects have high MAPE=82.5% due to small absolute magnitudes and confounding with the grand mean under binarization. Despite magnitude distortion, the ranking of systematic components is preserved (Spearman \u03c1=0.68 excl. residual), supporting the use of Henderson I for identifying dominant variance sources in binary LLM evaluation data."
